{"entryId":"1435","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1435:1","sourceSha256":"bdefd71e28f7c2c5d82cba5e9098769eb3c36fbeb250c4f577b67f801416fa0b","englishSha256":"60b7ab61823689164c7a9988cc06351bce5acdda8e96a54bd1f4e51d6a88334b","citations":[{"id":"1435:1:citation-01","he":[28,118],"en":[169,180],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_85b.9"},"reference":"Ketubot 85b:9","assessment":"Rava cites the father to his son, but the checked witness names that father Rav Chiyya bar Avin. The studenthood claim and received Chinena reading remain qualified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 85b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_85b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1435:1:citation-02","he":[120,177],"en":[230,241],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Keritot_20a.11"},"reference":"Keritot 20a:11","assessment":"The exact Bavli preserves Ammi and Chananyah and their common teaching.","evidence":[{"reference":"Keritot 20a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Keritot_20a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1435:1:citation-03","he":[179,251],"en":[318,329],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_86b.1"},"reference":"Shabbat 86b:1","assessment":"The three Bavli loci each have the two names in separate contexts. The Megillah side is confirmed, and the Shabbat spelling Ravin is kept visible.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 86b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_86b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Megillah 7b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_7b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 87b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_87b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1435:1:citation-04","he":[179,251],"en":[331,342],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_7b.6"},"